From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: keruth <keruth@local>
Date: Sun, 9 Nov 2026 08:40:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: cvitek: free the mailbox before resetting the core

`cvitek_rproc_stop()` reset the C906L and gated its clock while the mailbox
channels were still registered.  Those channels are what lets this side take
the CVITEK mailbox spinlock, and that spinlock is shared with the remote core:
a firmware gated in the middle of the critical section leaves it held, so the
next host access spins forever.  The symptom on the bench is a board that stops
answering entirely -- no panic, no USB, nothing in the log after the stop.

Free the channels first, so no host path can wait on the remote core, and only
then reset and gate it.  Combined with a page protocol that publishes through a
seqlock (`write_state`/`seq`), a core stopped at an arbitrary instruction is a
recoverable event instead of a hang.
---
 drivers/remoteproc/cvitek_remoteproc.c | 25 +++++++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/cvitek_remoteproc.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/cvitek_remoteproc.c
@@ -666,12 +666,17 @@
 
 	dev_dbg(&rproc->dev, "Stopping\n");
 
-	sw_err = cvitek_rproc_set_reset(rproc, true);
-	if (sw_err)
-		dev_err(&rproc->dev, "Failed to reset C906L\n");
-
-	clk_disable(ddata->clk);
-
+	/*
+	 * Detach the mailbox channels before the core is reset.
+	 *
+	 * While a channel is registered this side can still take the shared
+	 * CVITEK mailbox spinlock to post or read a message.  A remote core gated
+	 * in the middle of that critical section leaves the lock held, and the
+	 * next host access spins forever -- the symptom is a board that stops
+	 * answering with no panic.  Freeing the channels first removes every
+	 * host path that can wait on the remote core, so the reset below is safe
+	 * whatever the firmware was doing.
+	 */
 	if (ddata->mbox_chan[MBOX_RX]) {
 		mbox_free_channel(ddata->mbox_chan[MBOX_RX]);
 		ddata->mbox_chan[MBOX_RX] = NULL;
@@ -682,6 +687,12 @@
 	}
 
 
+	sw_err = cvitek_rproc_set_reset(rproc, true);
+	if (sw_err)
+		dev_err(&rproc->dev, "Failed to reset C906L\n");
+
+	clk_disable(ddata->clk);
+
 	return sw_err;
 }
 
